Feature Selection using Wrapper Method

Overview

This project applies wrapper-based feature selection on the Adult dataset using k-Nearest Neighbors (kNN) with forward selection.

Dataset

The Adult dataset is used for income classification (>50K vs. <=50K).

Preprocessing includes handling missing values, encoding categorical features, and shuffling.

Methodology

Preprocessing: Load and clean data, encode categorical variables, and convert labels (>50K → 1, <=50K → -1).

Feature Selection:

Start with an empty feature set S.

Iteratively add the feature x from F that maximizes balanced accuracy using kNN.

Stop when adding a new feature no longer improves accuracy.

Evaluation: Report selected features and accuracy for both income classes.

Dependencies

Install required libraries:

pip install numpy pandas scikit-learn

Running the Code

Load and preprocess the dataset.

Run the forward selection algorithm.

Evaluate the selected feature subset.

Results

The optimal feature subset is reported.

Accuracy for each class is analyzed.
